<title>ESTONIA: ESTONIAN BUSINESS GROUP AGINST ELECTRICITY PLAN - REPORT.</title>
<headline>ESTONIAN BUSINESS GROUP AGINST ELECTRICITY PLAN - REPORT.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Estonian chamber of commerce and industry said that the proposed business plan for the Narva power station should be put on hold, Aripaev newspaper said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The head of the chamber, Toomas Tamsar, was quoted as saying the plan, presented by U.S. based NRG Energy , Eesti Energy and the government, would push electricity prices unreasonably high.</p>
<p>--Tallinn newsroom +372 620 9202 reuters@reuters.ee</p>
</text>
